ok - boards come entirely from local configuration, and an unconfigured home has none
ok - with no board configured the bridge reads nothing, writes nothing, and creates nothing
ok - removing the configuration disables the bridge with no residue, and undoes nothing already done
ok - malformed board configuration is refused with the reason, not guessed around
ok - only a project with a configured board is mapped, and boards never cross
ok - intake takes real issues, in the first column, carrying the configured trigger
ok - the label is the authoritative trigger; mention and assignee stay off unless configured
ok - one issue holds one task: repeat import is a no-op and a conflicting relink is refused
ok - the linkage record lives with the durable fleet records and survives task cleanup
ok - Todo, In Progress, and Done are driven by dispatch and merge, on the board's own column names
ok - a column the adapter does not drive is reported by its own name, never adopted as a state
ok - the working PR is attached to the issue that started the work, once
ok - a blocker is recorded on the issue while the item stays visible where it is
ok - a status firstmate did not write is reported and changes nothing on either side
ok - the queued column is written from firstmate's records, and a card it did not place starts nothing
ok - with no queued key configured the column does not exist in either direction
ok - a withdrawn card is reported until reconciled, and never costs unlanded work
ok - archiving a finished card is ordinary housekeeping, not a withdrawal
ok - board writes degrade to a stale board and reconcile on the next cycle
ok - an unreadable board is reported and retried, never mistaken for withdrawn work
ok - a board that answers with nothing while links are open is reported, not obeyed
ok - a page boundary is never mistaken for absence
ok - an intake filter decides what is importable, never what is still on the board
ok - an issue another board owns is named and left alone, never silently re-homed
ok - an outstanding PR attachment is retried until the issue has it, then left alone
ok - a single-card event resolves its card from the issue and never reads the board
ok - a board with nothing to act on polls to no output, and --all still lists it
ok - poll confirms a write the board already shows, without printing or writing
ok - what an invocation costs is set by the work it does, never by the board's size
ok - with no container columns configured nothing about decomposition exists
ok - a half-configured or self-overlapping container lane is refused, never half-enabled
ok - a labelled container is offered for decomposition, and container and task can never be the same issue
ok - a container is decomposed once, ever, and the record outlives the work
ok - a child is created labelled, linked to its parent, carded in Todo, and never re-imported
